LIKEOS-EFIBOOT(1)            System Administration           LIKEOS-EFIBOOT(1)

NAME
       likeos-efiboot - show and edit the firmware's boot entries

SYNOPSIS
       likeos-efiboot [--list] [-v]
       likeos-efiboot  --create --disk dev --part n --loader path --label text
       [--first] [--options text]
       likeos-efiboot --delete num
       likeos-efiboot --active num | --inactive num
       likeos-efiboot --bootorder num,num,...  [--force]
       likeos-efiboot --bootnext num | --delete-bootnext
       likeos-efiboot --timeout seconds | --delete-timeout

DESCRIPTION
       likeos-efiboot shows and changes the boot entries of a computer's  UEFI
       firmware:  the  list  the firmware's boot menu offers, and the order in
       which it tries them when nobody chooses.

       The firmware keeps these settings in UEFI variables of the  EFI  global
       variable  GUID:  Boot#### (one load option per entry: whether it is ac-
       tive, its label, the device path of the loader it starts, and  optional
       data  passed  to  the loader), BootOrder (the entries in the order they
       are tried), BootNext (one  entry  to  try  on  the  next  start  only),
       BootCurrent (the entry the running system was started from) and Timeout
       (how  many  seconds  the  firmware's own menu waits).  The kernel shows
       every variable as a file in /sys/firmware/efi/efivars;  on  a  computer
       started without UEFI, or with efi=noruntime on the kernel command line,
       the  directory  does  not exist and likeos-efiboot says so (exit status
       2).

       Without an action, or with --list, the entries are shown:  BootCurrent,
       BootNext,  the timeout and the boot order, then one line per entry with
       its number, an asterisk when it is active, its  label  and  the  device
       path  of the loader it starts.  With -v each entry's attributes and op-
       tional data are shown too.

       Several actions may be given at once; they run  in  the  order  create,
       delete,  active/inactive,  bootorder,  bootnext, timeout.  Changing the
       variables needs root.

ACTIONS
       --list Show the boot entries (the default).

       -c, --create
              Create a boot entry for a loader on an EFI system partition,  as
              a   freshly   installed   system  needs  one:  the  device  path
              HD(n,GPT,guid,start,size)/File(loader) is taken from the  parti-
              tion table of the disk given with --disk, and the entry gets the
              label given with --label.  An entry that already starts the same
              loader  from the same partition is reused rather than duplicated
              (and given the new label and options).   Needs  --disk,  --part,
              --loader and --label.

       -B, --delete num
              Delete entry num and take it out of the boot order.

       -a, --active num
              Mark entry num active: the firmware tries it.

       -A, --inactive num
              Mark  entry  num inactive: it stays in the list but the firmware
              passes over it.

       -o, --bootorder num,num,...
              Set the boot order.  Numbers of entries that do  not  exist  are
              refused unless --force is given.

       -n, --bootnext num
              Start  entry  num  on  the next start only; the firmware deletes
              BootNext when it uses it.

       -N, --delete-bootnext
              Cancel BootNext.

       -t, --timeout seconds
              Set how long the firmware's own boot menu waits.

       -T, --delete-timeout
              Remove the timeout setting (the firmware's default applies).

CREATE OPTIONS
       -d, --disk dev
              The  disk  that  holds  the  EFI  system  partition   (/dev/sda,
              /dev/nvme0n1).

       -p, --part n
              The number of the EFI system partition on it.

       -l, --loader path
              The   loader's   path   on  that  partition,  with  backslashes:
              \EFI\LIKEOS\BOOTX64.EFI.

       -L, --label text
              The name the firmware's boot menu shows.

       -f, --first
              Put the entry first in the boot order (otherwise it is added  at
              the end).

       -u, --options text
              Optional data passed to the loader (as UCS-2 text).

OPTIONS
       --force
              Accept entry numbers in --bootorder that have no entry.

       -q, --quiet
              Report errors only.

       -v, --verbose
              Show the attributes and optional data of the entries too.

       -h, --help
              Show a summary of the actions and options.

       --version
              Show the version.

       num  is  a  hexadecimal entry number: 3, 0003 and Boot0003 are the same
       entry.

EXIT STATUS
       0      Success.

       1      The action failed.

       2      Wrong usage, or the system has no UEFI variables.

ENVIRONMENT
       LIKEOS_EFIVARS_DIR
              A directory used  in  place  of  /sys/firmware/efi/efivars  (for
              tests).

FILES
       /sys/firmware/efi/efivars/Name-GUID
              One UEFI variable: four bytes of attributes (little-endian) fol-
              lowed  by  its value.  Writing the file in one write(2) sets the
              variable, unlink(2) deletes it.

EXAMPLES
       The entry the installer creates for a  LikeOS  installation  whose  EFI
       system partition is the first partition of /dev/nvme0n1:

              likeos-efiboot --create --disk /dev/nvme0n1 --part 1 \
                      --loader '\EFI\LIKEOS\BOOTX64.EFI' \
                      --label LikeOS --first

       Start entry 0004 once, on the next start:

              likeos-efiboot --bootnext 4

SEE ALSO
       likeos-install(1), likeos-gpt(1)

